Z||000012||MR2KLR||10-27-2001||02:20 AM||||I used too own a Turbo 84SE with a 2.5L duke all done up "right" I bought i like that from a used car dealer ship. It was damn quick! It was taged and legel for a month and was driven 4 days a total of about 100 miles in that time the car sufferd fom (4) blown head gaskets (2) bad water pumps (2) sets of fouled plugs and a blown apart TBI & EGR valve until the last time so much anti-freze got in the berings it just locked up and so it sits (less turbo I sold that to a friend) It was a homemade system that was just a hacked & welded 2.5L Fiero manifold with a Garret TD04 (thats right! TD04= Typhoon/Cyclone 4.3L) turbo welded to the manifold and pre-fab exhaust pipe & 3" std intake pipeing runing to a stock 4-tech air cleaner houseing and a mech. boost gauge mounted on a plate where the radio went. It was awful and me being a 16 year old kid (4 yrs ago) worked up every penny of the $3500 window price! I still have the car, though I have parted it all out ( my mother lost the title) so it just sits there to laugh at me every day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> the car still only has 53K original miles on it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I am depresed now The duke can be pepy or even quick but never truly fast||||reg||13
